This repository contains no third-party code or model weights. install.sh
downloads and installs the following, each under its own license:

- Kokoro-82M voice model and voices, by hexgrad
  https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M — Apache License 2.0
  Fetched at revision f3ff3571791e39611d31c381e3a41a3af07b4987 and checked
  against models.sha256.
- kokoro and misaki Python packages, by hexgrad — Apache License 2.0
- PyTorch — Apache-2.0 AND BSD-2-Clause AND BSD-3-Clause AND BSL-1.0 AND MIT
  (with LLVM-exception), per its package metadata
- spaCy en_core_web_sm language model, by Explosion — MIT License
- numpy — BSD-3-Clause (bundled parts: 0BSD, MIT, Zlib, CC0-1.0)
- soundfile — BSD-3-Clause

- espeak-ng library and data (GPL-3.0-or-later), bundled inside the
  espeakng_loader package that misaki depends on; kokoro uses it for words
  outside misaki's dictionary.

Other dependencies pip installs along the way include copyleft and
weak-copyleft packages, used unmodified as published on PyPI:
- phonemizer-fork — GPL-3.0-or-later (via misaki)
- num2words — LGPL
- libsndfile — LGPL-2.1, bundled inside the soundfile package
- certifi — MPL-2.0; tqdm — MPL-2.0 AND MIT
The remaining dependencies are under permissive licenses (MIT, BSD, Apache).
Listen Book's own code links to none of them at build time and redistributes
none of them; it is MIT-licensed.
